Option: season-picker-off
Name: seasonPicker: false (no "See the farm in..." preview buttons for visitors)
Does: Sets seasonPicker to false in js/content.js, so every visitor sees the season the calendar says and nothing to click between seasons. Many tests look at or click that switcher (hero, games, keyboard, calm, privacy, forced-colors, auto-dark, no-js, and dated, analytics, i18n-early) and would fail with it gone, so the patch also changes tests/lib.mjs: every page a test opens has the switcher switched on, except where a test writes js/content.js itself (the seasonPicker: false part of hero does).
Answers: launch decision D6 (checklist 3.8; the playbook mentions it in the list of launch decisions)
Profile: filled (only tried in the settings-filled run of the matrix, not multiplied into every combination)
Conflicts: none
Requires: none
Host: any
Order: 5
After: nothing to rebuild; upload again
Strings: none

